# Every message is one run. The FIRST message the page sends is
# {"type":"connect","service":"echo"}; parse it so the connect op can read
# the service name. Once the session is bound the chassis stops making runs
# for this socket — the service's frames go straight through — so this
# parse only ever sees the one connect message (and any the page sends
# after a detach).
WHEN @websocket.phase == "message" && @websocket.msg.text != ""
  EMIT .msg = &json(@websocket.msg.text)
